    <item>
      <title>A Call to Chapel with the Rev. Frederick D. Haynes III, Ph.D. (in-person and virtual)| Homecoming 2026 at Cramton Auditorium</title>
      <description><![CDATA[<div>  <img src="https://localist-images.azureedge.net/photos/53737283626131/huge/829ba0381ab871990cc95254fd2db9bf6f09e777.jpg" style="width: 100%;" />  <div style="font-size: 0.9em; color: #555;"><strong>Sun, 18 Oct 2026</strong></div>  <div><p>The Rev. Dr. Frederick Douglass Haynes, III, is a prophetic pastor, passionate leader, social activist, eloquent orator, and educator engaged in preaching the gospel of Jesus Christ, and fighting against racial injustice. Dr. Haynes is also committed to and has devoted his life to economic justice and empowerment in underserved communities and touching and transforming the lives of the disenfranchised. For the past 40 years, Dr. Haynes has served as a visionary and innovative senior pastor of Friendship-West Baptist Church in Dallas, Texas. Under his servant leadership, the ministry and membership of the church has grown from less than 100 members in 1983 to over 13,000.</p>

<p> </p>

<p>To learn more about our guest speaker, click here.</p>

